{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Outside the curtain of the Testimony</b> — and likewise it is written (Exodus 27:21) 'which is over the Testimony,' and this is what the Sages said: the western lamp is a testimony that the Shekhinah is among Israel." "<b>Outside the curtain</b> — the verse begins with mem and ends with mem, for the Hall was forty cubits long (and likewise the curtain, its measure was forty)." "<b>Aaron shall arrange it</b> — and elsewhere it is written 'Aaron and his sons,' because after Nadav and Avihu died upon entering the Hall, Aaron did not let his sons enter alone but would enter with them; nevertheless, he would withdraw at the time of the burning of the incense."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:25.775122997Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}